    "blurb": "Stage spotlights cut through the dark as players fire confetti cannons and trigger sky drops, sending thousands of shimmering 3D flakes tumbling through beams of light.",
    "prompt": "The moment the confetti drops at a concert: anyone can fire a cannon in their colour, blasting thousands of shimmering flakes that flutter, spin and catch the light as they fall across the stage lights. Make it striking on a big projected wall in a dark room: a bold composition, rich colour against real blacks, depth, glow, and motion that reads from across the room. Keep a demoscener's economy: lookup tables and fixed-size buffers kept in room.state, low-resolution offscreen buffers for any per-pixel work, nothing allocated inside hot loops, a steady 60fps at 1920x1080, and compact, clearly named code.",
